! AlAs, ultrasoft, on an **unshifted** 2x2x2 grid **reduced to its wedge**: half of
! the pair that says a Born charge's wedge sum has been completed.
!
! Its partner is `alas-epsilon-us-unshifted-nosym.in`, the same cell and the same
! k-sample run whole with the symmetrisation switched off. An unshifted grid is
! closed under the point group, so the two are the same sample by two routes and
! agreeing is the only check `symmetrize_directional` has at this order -- QE
! computes the reduced route alone.
!
! **The crystal is polar and the dataset is augmented, and both are needed for the
! pair to say anything.** On a centrosymmetric cell `Z*` is zero by symmetry, so
! what the two routes agree about is the sum-rule residue and not the charge; and
! at frozen wavefunctions the density moves with the atoms only when `S` does, so
! the term that fails to complete -- `int (drho/du) K (drho/dE)`, a product of two
! per-k tangents -- does not exist on a norm-conserving dataset at all.
!
! **2x2x2 is deliberate and is not a converged sample.** The charges come out near
! 0.27 and -8.63 rather than near 2, which makes the comparison absolute rather
! than a cancellation between two large numbers, and it keeps the pair inside the
! slow suite's budget: the whole-grid half is eight k-points rather than the
! sixty-four an unshifted 4x4x4 would need.
!
! Cell, cutoffs and datasets are `alas-epsilon-us.in`'s.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.575, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98  Al.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
 As  74.92  As.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 2 2 2 0 0 0
